+## Context
+
+New TypeScript project (strict, ESM, NodeNext), no source yet, no runtime dependency. Tests use `node --test`; Node 22 strips TypeScript types natively, so tests import `../src/index.ts` directly.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** a small in-memory rental service obeying the school's rules. **Non-Goals:** cancellations, persistence, season enforcement.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Everything lives in `src/index.ts` (no relative imports inside `src`, since `.js`-suffixed imports would not resolve under native type stripping). Only erasable TypeScript syntax is used (no enums, parameter properties).
+- Times are parsed with a strict regex for `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS(.sss)?Z` then `Date.parse`, and require a round-trip check so impossible dates are rejected; midnight is checked on the epoch ms (`% 86_400_000 === 0`). Whole days = `(end - start) / 86_400_000`. UTC has no DST, so days are exact.
+- Returned `start`/`end` are echoed as given by the caller.
+- Money: `dailyPrice` must be a non-negative safe integer; `total = dailyPrice * days`, which must stay a safe integer.
+- Overlap: half-open intervals `[start, end)`; two overlap iff `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`. Bookings are kept per item in a Map.
+- Booking ids: sequential `"booking-N"` strings from a counter.
+- Cancellation: not implemented; the 24h rule is recorded in the spec only.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Season (April–October) is not enforced, as the request does not ask for it; recorded as out of scope.
