+## Why
+
+The booking desk of the Lakeside Windsurf School has no way to rent out boards and sails to students and visitors. The desk needs a first, basic rental module: register equipment, quote a rental, and book it without double-booking.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createRentalService()`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an in-memory rental service.
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })` registers a board or a sail with a daily price in euro cents.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })` returns the total cost of renting an item for a period.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })` books the item for a free period and returns the booking.
+- The rules apply everywhere: integer euro cents, UTC ISO-8601 times, whole-day periods at midnight UTC, no overlapping bookings of one item.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope: rentals of boards and sails at the booking desk (rentals, not lessons or customers); quoting and booking; validation of items and periods; the in-memory store.
+
+Out of scope: cancellations and refunds (the policy — no refund under 24 hours before start, full refund otherwise — is a standing school rule that a later change will implement), lessons, customers, persistence, season (April to October) enforcement, discounts.
+
+## Impact
+
+- New file `src/index.ts` and tests under `test/`.
+- No runtime dependency is introduced; only TypeScript and the Node standard library.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `rental`: equipment registration, quoting and booking of rentals.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+None.
